' QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: What must be verified before one application is drawn as integrated with another?
' SOURCES: Reference enterprise architecture model (proposed)
' GENERAL KNOWLEDGE / conceptual schema; not statutory structure
@startuml
title 16j Authority, source-of-record and integration distinction
skinparam shadowing false
component "Authorizing institution
(mandate, instrument)" as Auth
component "System of record A
(specific entity + period)" as A
component "Agency application B
(user data / output)" as B
interface "Interface evidence
(schema / logs / owner)" as I
component "Manual transfer / portal
(if used)" as M
component "Reconciliation evidence
(matched IDs and balances)" as R
Auth --> A : creates/controls mandate
A --> I : observed exchange only if verified
I --> B : production/pilot/planned
status required
A --> M : alternative route
M --> B : re-entry / upload
B --> R : compare receiving record
A --> R : authoritative original
note bottom of I
Name, environment, protocol, payload,
owner, dates and audit evidence.
Do not infer a live API from both
systems appearing in an architecture.
end note
@enduml
